# Scene audit runner implementation (3 October 2026)

- API: createSceneAuditRunner({ hythonPath, auditScriptPath, timeoutMs }, { execFile? } = {}) returns run(scenePath, { signal } = {}). Injected execFile is asynchronous, compatible with promisify(node:child_process.execFile). (3 October 2026)
- Each request waits behind the preceding audit; a rejected job releases the queue. The runner uses asynchronous execFile with separate script, scene and --output arguments. No shell, scheduling, main-loop blocking, backend change or scene source write. (3 October 2026)
- A private mkdtemp directory receives audit.json and is removed in finally on success, nonzero exit, timeout, cancellation or invalid output. The configurable timeout and independent AbortSignal kill the headless child with SIGKILL. A signal already aborted rejects before launch. (3 October 2026)
- Exit stderr is retained in a bounded useful error. JSON must be readable and carry schemaVersion 1, a SHA256-shaped sceneSha256, references array and portabilityVerified false. The service remains responsible for comparing the hash with current scene bytes. No evidence is synthesized. (3 October 2026)
- Verification: npx vitest run scripts/Assets/SceneAuditRunner.test.js passes 8 tests on 3 October 2026 at 04:24 Europe/Paris. Real Node executable fixtures prove separated arguments, returned JSON, cleanup, nonzero exit, invalid JSON/evidence, timeout and AbortSignal cancellation. An injected executable proves serialized jobs, event-loop progress and queue recovery after failure. (3 October 2026)
